    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0885" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg785"/>

                <head>No. 497.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Señor Navarro.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 27,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s note to you
                    of the 23d ultimo, regarding certain unofficial rumors of intended invasion of
                    Mexican territory by raiding parties, and wherein were quoted the telegraphic
                    instructions to the United States military authorities to prevent any violation
                    of the neutrality laws by armed forces, I have now the honor to communicate to
                    you, for the information of the government you represent, that I am advised, by
                    a letter from the War Department of the 8th instant, that the forces which
                    General Marquez had collected had been disbanded in consequence of the action of
                    our military authorities.</p>
                <p>Should your government receive any information of any movement <pb facs="0886"
                        n="786" xml:id="pg786"/> of General Marquez towards a renewal of his
                    projected invasion, it will be the desire of this government promptly to take
                    measures to frustrate it.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c., &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
